  ^^^^^^^^
Assign it to a name, as in `const label = case ...`, or give each `when` a block in braces in place of `then`.
diagnostics/case-syntax.em:27:24: a `case` used as a value gives each `when` a value with `then`
  const block_as_value = case 1 {
                         ^^^^^^^^
Write `when ... then value` for each arm, and `else then value`, or use the `case` as a statement on its own line.
diagnostics/case-syntax.em:33:5: expected `when` or `else` in this `case`, found a name
      print(1)
      ^^^^^
Each arm of a `case` starts with `when` and what it matches, as in `when 1 { ... }`.
diagnostics/case-syntax.em:36:1: this `case` has no `when` arms
  case 1 {
  ^^^^^^^^
Add an arm for each value to match, as in `when 1 { ... }`.
diagnostics/case-syntax.em:40:19: expected the end of the arm, found else
